  youtubeSummary="One thing most people get wrong when using this tool: using EBITDA as a direct proxy for cash flow. The correct approach is: EBITDA ignores capital expenditure, which can be substantial especially for asset-heavy businesses. Pair it with capex data to get a cleaner picture of actual cash generation."
  metaTitle="EBITDA Calculator | Formula, Examples & Steps"
  description="Calculate EBITDA from Net Income + Interest + Tax + D&A (bottom-up) or from Revenue - COGS - OpEx excl. D&A (top-down). Step-by-step workings and EBITDA Margin."
